WEBVTT

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.460
The snow of winter is going away gradually

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.900
and spring is visiting the land again.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:47.520
The spring breeze is running through the
fields and mountains of Prince Edward Island.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.490
Bright River!

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.080
The train departs!

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:08.960
The cherry blossoms are early
this year, don't you think?

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.720
Where are you going?

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.780
I'm going to Carmody, Mr. Station Master.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.950
Will someone pick you up?

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:17.790
Yes, my father is supposed to pick me up.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:22.820
Really? The Carmody branch will be
opened next week.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.600
It will be more convenient then.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:29.840
I know. Right now, everyone in Carmody
is busy preparing to welcome it.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.550
I guess so.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.300
Could that be my father?

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.730
Father!

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.650
Goodbye, Mr. Station Master.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.480
Goodbye.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:51.480
I remember another girl like her who
got off the train alone a long time ago.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:55.950
I think she sat here,
waiting for someone to pick her up...

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:04.190
Four years have passed since Anne
came to Green Gables in a carriage

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:08.160
from Bright River Station with Matthew.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.220
Anne is now fifteen years old.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.470
Marilla, I'm back.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:16.970
Welcome back. You're back early today.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:26.680
Anne.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:28.310
What is it, Marilla?

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.550
When did you grown so tall?

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:35.550
Why are you asking such
strange questions, Marilla?

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:36.820
But...

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.560
You've really grown up, Anne.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.930
Well, I'm fifteen years old now.
It's obvious that I would grow taller, right?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.410
Fifteen...

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:57.540
Oh yes, Marilla, what are you doing
with my old clothes?

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:59.050
These?

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:04.680
I meant to use them as material for patchwork,
but it seems like such a waste.

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:08.300
You wore these clothes when you first came to us.

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.380
There are too many memories
in them, don't you think?

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.010
Please let me hold it.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:16.100
Oh, it's so small.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:24.000
Marilla, to think I wore such
small clothes in the past.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:31.880
That night, Anne and Diana attended
a prayer meeting together.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.440
Marilla, who sits alone at home in the darkness,

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:38.330
feels a strange disappointment
that Anne has grown so tall.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:43.720
When did the little child, that
Marilla loved so much, disappear?

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:51.560
In her place, a tall, 15-year old girl
with a serious look has appeared.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:06.600
Well, well, there's no need to cry so about it.

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:09.780
Yes, there is need!

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:11.620
You would cry, too!

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:18.060
If you were an orphan and had come to a
place you thought was going to be home,

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.840
and found they didn't want you
because you weren't a boy,

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.900
Aunty would cry, too.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:28.230
Oh, this is the most tragical thing
that ever happened to me!

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:35.700
Well, don't cry any more. We're not going to
turn you out-of-doors tonight.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:39.100
What is your name?

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:47.450
Will you please call me Cordelia?

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:51.890
Call you Cordelia?
Is that your name?

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:56.020
Well, um... it's not exactly my name,

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.620
but I would love to be called Cordelia.

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:01.830
It's such a perfectly elegant name.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:05.860
I don't know what on earth you mean.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:11.070
If Cordelia isn't your name, what is?

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:14.420
Anne Shirley...

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.420
Anne Shirley...

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:21.660
Marilla vividly remembers how Anne's voice sounded at that time.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:24.580
While the love she had
poured into that child

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:27.170
is the same love she is now
pouring into the current Anne,

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:30.810
she can't help feeling an unspeakable loneliness

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:34.040
and a deep sadness that she has lost something.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:42.560
Matthew.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:45.590
What is it?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.760
Oh, it's nothing...

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:56.770
I saw you crying, so...

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:02.710
I'm all right, I was just thinking about Anne.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.150
- About Anne?
- Yes.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:08.280
That child has really grown up.

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:12.380
Another three months and she
will be leaving this place.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:15.590
I'm sure she will pass the
examinations to get into Queen's.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:18.650
When I think of this, I feel so lonely.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:29.270
She will come back often.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:33.510
In a week, we will be able
to go to Carmody by train.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:37.540
Then Charlottetown will not seem so far away.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:38.750
Well, well.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:43.150
Matthew, do you still treat her as
the little girl from four years ago?

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:47.750
But that child will not stay by our sides forever.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:50.020
Well...

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:56.230
Anyway, you men won't
understand that kind of thing.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:59.790
Oh no, I forgot to light the candles.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:02.240
I'll get the tea ready right away.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.370
Anne is not the only one who has changed.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:11.200
The windows of Anne's East Bay room,

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:15.330
which were bare four years ago,
are completely transformed.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:21.680
As Anne has grown up, it has taken
on the atmosphere of a young girl's room.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.770
Anne, how much longer will the big
remodeling for your room take?

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.570
It's almost done.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:36.840
And the new bed that Matthew
bought me will arrive today.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.640
Oh my! I want to see that, too!

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.610
Anne, what does big remodeling mean?

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:44.190
It means Anne's room will be prettier.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:47.980
On 'Train Day',
Aunt Josephine's coming to our place.

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:49.930
- Really, Diana?
- Yes.

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:52.930
When we came back from the prayer
meeting last night, a telegram had come.

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:58.590
That's great! It's been a long time.
But what is this 'Train Day'?

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.430
It's the day the railway branch
has its opening ceremony.

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:05.430
Minnie May does not understand that,
so she keeps saying 'Train Day'.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:09.470
Oh, I see. You'll be picking up
Miss Barry that day, won't you?

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:12.640
Of course. Anne, aren't you going?

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:17.710
It's not likely that I can go.
Queens class has a lesson that day.

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:25.090
Of course I'm attending the opening
ceremony of the railway service.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:29.390
This is very important for both Carmody and Avonlea.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:33.580
They say that many important people from
Charlottetown will come on that day.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:36.530
There's no way I will miss it!

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:42.670
By the way, when is Anne's new bed coming?

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:48.110
Matthew and Jerry have gone for it.
They should be back soon.

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:52.210
Aren't you indulging Anne a little too much?

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:55.380
Maybe it is as you say, Rachel,

00:10:55.580 --> 00:11:01.160
but the two of us would like to do as
much as we possibly can for now.

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:06.110
Now that you mention it,
she's become very quiet.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:08.830
Is she still as keen on studying as before?

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:15.070
The Queen's exams are near. She seems
to have studied until late last night.

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:19.370
She looks calm, but I'm sure
she worries a lot about it.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.860
Jerry, please untie the rope.

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:38.760
All right.

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:41.950
Oh my! Here it is!

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.700
It's a very good one!

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:46.400
I've never seen such a beautiful bed.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:49.830
We're moving this to the 2nd floor, right? I'll help, too.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:50.300
Huh?

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:52.370
Now, Matthew, you go and rest.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:55.170
Heavy lifting is not good for your heart, right?

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:57.650
But, I...

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:06.480
Oh my! My bed is here already!

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.600
Oh...

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:15.730
Anne, don't just stand there and
admire it. Come and help!

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:16.830
Eh? Yes!

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:20.890
Sorry to trouble all of you.

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:47.260
Anne, can I come in?

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:48.550
Yes, please do.

00:12:49.730 --> 00:12:51.820
Anne, I am taking away the candle.

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:52.630
Okay.

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:03.540
Neat and clean. It looks more and
more like a girl's room.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:04.910
Yes.

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:07.360
Thank you for the beautiful bed.

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:22.920
Anne.

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:24.060
What is it?

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:27.130
You don't talk half as much as you used to,

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:30.800
and you don't blurt out
big words like before either.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:33.140
What happened?

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.240
I don't know either.

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:37.650
I don't want to talk as much.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:40.870
If I have any good ideas or pleasant thoughts,

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:44.850
I put them gently within my heart.
Like jewels.

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:51.590
I don't like to have them laughed at or wondered over.

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:58.060
And somehow I don't want to use big words any more.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.700
But I feel a bit lonely,

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:03.800
because I've become so grown up.

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:07.610
I should be able to use them whenever I want.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:14.640
It's fun to be almost grown up in some ways,
but it's not the kind of fun I expected, Marilla.

00:14:41.090 --> 00:14:43.650
Anne's entrance examinations are near.

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:45.430
Yes.

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:54.780
We should consider her lodgings during
the period of her exams.

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:59.560
Well now, but we don't know any one in Charlottetown.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:04.970
Anne says Queen's Academy provides
lodgings for examinees.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:10.040
I think I'll apply for those.

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:11.870
Well now...

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:17.610
It makes no difference to me.
It's up to how she feels about it.

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:23.210
Let's discuss this with Miss Stacy
before deciding. You come, too.

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:41.330
Miss Stacy, can we talk?

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:46.140
Quiet down.
Revise on your own for now.

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:51.340
Anne, what's the matter?

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:52.640
I don't know.

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:01.960
Anne, I wish you could come to Carmody as well.

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:05.520
I'm really sorry. Please give my best regards to Miss Barry.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:10.610
Everyone, the railroad branch
has extended to Carmody.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:13.430
Do you know that the first train is coming through today?

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:14.460
Yes!

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:17.740
The committee has informed us

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:20.540
to let elementary school students in and around Carmody

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.570
go and welcome this memorable train.

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:27.440
Quiet down.

00:16:27.490 --> 00:16:30.340
Since we will be going to Carmody now,

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:32.500
today's lessons will end here.

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:34.190
Hurray!

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:37.180
- That's great!
- Yes!

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:51.100
Thank you.

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:52.970
Sorry to trouble you.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:55.380
This is wonderfully convenient.

00:16:55.410 --> 00:17:01.350
My daughter married a man in Carmody.
With this, I'll be able to visit her more often.

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:04.620
My niece and her family are in Avonlea, too.

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:08.020
That's right! You must be looking forward to it, right?

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:10.990
That is not the only thing
I am looking forward to.

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:48.050
It's running late.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:49.660
I'm sure it'll be here soon.

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:54.380
This train will carry my Aunt Josephine.
She'll bring many gifts.

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:55.840
- Here it is!
- Here's the train!

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:03.470
Here it comes! Here's the first train!

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:12.900
There's Aunt Josephine!

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:17.720
Aunt Josephine! Over here!

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:21.130
Diana, Minnie May and Anne!

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:24.290
Aunt Josephine! Aunt Josephine!

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:42.810
Aren't you joining the celebration?

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:45.380
I'm not going to waste my time on this.

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:48.720
Aunt Josephine! Aunt!

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:51.690
Little one, how are you?

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:54.100
I'm fine. Did you bring us presents?

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:56.080
Yes. Lots.

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:58.510
How do you do, Aunt Josephine.

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:03.110
How do you do, Miss Josephine Barry?

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:06.510
Oh my... Is this Anne Shirley?

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:18.950
Anne, you've grown up a lot
and become prettier, too.

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:24.300
Thank you, Miss Barry, but I haven't changed that much.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:26.460
No, you've changed a lot.

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:31.590
The first time I saw you,
your sharp tongue was interesting.

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:35.000
Please don't say that. It's embarrassing.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:38.630
Well, how was the train ride, Aunt Josephine?

00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:44.270
Oh, it was comfortable, but I still don't trust trains much.

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:46.880
Still, it was surprisingly good.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.720
It was much easier than
taking a horse-drawn carriage.

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:52.990
If only there was less soot and smoke.

00:19:52.990 --> 00:19:54.020
Oh my!

00:19:58.330 --> 00:20:01.460
So, how long does Miss Barry intend to stay?

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:05.440
Well, perhaps she will stay
here and relax for a while?

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:07.530
I had so much fun today!

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:11.510
I've met Miss Barry and seen a train
again after such a long time.

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:13.380
The exams are near.

00:20:13.470 --> 00:20:14.430
If not for something this big,

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:17.000
I wouldn't have been able
to take a break from studying.

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:19.110
Thanks to this, I feel motivated again!

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:23.180
Anne, if it's convenient for Miss Barry,

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:27.180
I would like to invite her to tea
tomorrow. What do you think?

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:32.750
I want to thank her for looking after
you when you went to Charlottetown.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:35.430
I'm all for it, Marilla!

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:38.350
I will prepare a feast with all my heart!

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:44.210
Miss Josephine Barry agrees
readily to the invitation.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:47.940
Anne starts to prepare
her best dishes immediately.

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:51.810
Marilla's offer to help is politely refused.

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:58.360
Besides wanting to serve Miss Barry
dishes she prepared herself,

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:05.160
it is a welcome distraction for Anne,
who has been preparing hard for the exam.

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:14.370
- Anne.
- Eh?

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.910
I think I should help you, after all.

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:20.330
It's all right. Leave everything to me today.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:24.780
Next, I'll just put the layer cake in the oven.

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:45.870
Anne Shirley!

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:51.440
What on earth did you
put into that cake?

00:21:51.680 --> 00:21:53.140
Vanilla.

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:56.200
Go and bring me the bottle
of vanilla you used.

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:02.120
It's really vanilla.

00:22:02.150 --> 00:22:03.780
Let me see.

00:22:12.980 --> 00:22:14.100
Mercy on us.

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:19.970
Anne, you've flavored that cake
with anodyne liniment.

00:22:24.020 --> 00:22:25.420
What is it, Marilla?

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:32.540
Nothing, I just thought of the past.

00:22:34.070 --> 00:22:38.950
The next day, Miss Barry visits
Green Gables along with Diana.

00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:44.920
Matthew welcomes Miss Barry
with such a nervous look,

00:22:45.170 --> 00:22:49.490
that Marilla is secretly worried about his heart.

00:22:50.630 --> 00:22:53.630
After Miss Barry has sampled the
delicious dishes Anne has prepared,

00:22:53.820 --> 00:22:56.800
she says to Marilla with satisfaction:

00:22:57.810 --> 00:22:59.490
- Marilla.
- Eh?

00:23:00.110 --> 00:23:02.170
May I call you Marilla?

00:23:02.450 --> 00:23:05.700
Anne's entrance examinations will start in July, right?

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:07.510
Yes, that's right.

00:23:07.700 --> 00:23:12.640
What do you think of letting Anne stay
with me during the examinations?

00:23:17.660 --> 00:23:22.560
I'm the most familiar thing to Anne in
the whole of Charlottetown.

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:25.690
Don't you think this is
the best arrangement, Marilla?

00:23:26.180 --> 00:23:30.170
If it's fine with Anne,
of course we have no objections.

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:31.800
Then that settles it.

00:23:31.990 --> 00:23:33.560
Anne, do you have any objections?

00:23:33.660 --> 00:23:35.540
No, I don't.

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:37.340
If you like,

00:23:37.380 --> 00:23:41.610
you can stay at my house and go to
Queen's Academy from there.

00:23:41.840 --> 00:23:45.950
Thank you so much for that.
But I have to pass the examinations first.

00:23:46.620 --> 00:23:52.320
You cannot possibly fail!
That's what I believe.

00:23:57.400 --> 00:24:00.950
Anne is overwhelmed by happiness

00:24:01.070 --> 00:24:03.530
as she is wrapped in the affection
of the people around her.

00:24:03.730 --> 00:24:11.620
She decides that she will pass the
entrance examinations in July with high scores.

00:24:17.780 --> 00:24:20.350
